The task is to develop a Python program that can find the optimal solution for minimizing regret-ratio problem, which involves finding a set of tuples from a database that are as close as possible to an ideal maxima representative (the one with minimum maximum regret). The Parent has developed two algorithms: 2D-RRMS and HD-RRMS. These algorithms guarantee a user controllable distance from the optimal solution in high-dimensional databases.

The linearithmic algorithm for minimizing regret ratio is called HD-RRMS, which guarantees a regret ratio that is within a user-controllable distance from the optimal regret ratio. The dynamic programming algorithm 2D-RRMS builds an optimal index to build the optimal index and runs in linearithmic time.
